    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into the August 30 slate with a primary offensive engine fueled by favorable park factors and exploitable matchups. **Gunnar Henderson** leads the charge with a 71.91 efficiency score; despite a challenging platoon disadvantage against Jeffrey Springs, the combination of a high-ceiling park environment and Springs' elevated xERA of 4.97 keeps him as our most potent asset. **Drake Baldwin** follows closely at 70.41, bolstered by his prime leadoff slot and a soft matchup against M. Adams, while **Kyle Tucker** (70.18) remains a high-floor selection despite the left-on-left confrontation with Framber Valdez. We are also looking for a breakout from **Coby Mayo** (66.72), who benefits from a rare positive platoon adjustment against Springs, highlighting the importance of the park effect in his upside.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was leaving **Miguel Vargas** on the sidelines. His efficiency score of 55.38 was respectable, driven by an impressive 0.390 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against Matthews, but he ultimately failed to clear the threshold set by the current starters who possess higher categorical utility today. Meanwhile, we are monitoring significant volatility for **Luis Robert Jr.**; while his score of 56.36 reflects a massive SP matchup advantage against Ethan Pecko, a 32% rain risk necessitates close attention to weather reports prior to first pitch. We are also tracking potential lineup fluctuations for **Jackson Merrill**, **Tommy White**, and **Gunnar Henderson**; while we have assumed their positions for this projection, any drop in the batting order would necessitate a re-evaluation of their daily efficiency scores.",
